{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod","id":293308,"title":"How to Decamp CWOD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-26T17:15:33-07:00","id":293308,"title":"How to Decamp CWOD?","content":"Any ideas on Rule changes and aspects to emphasize or deemphasize, if I want a more serious and less campy CWOD?<br /> <br /> Saw several ideas on &quot;Removing the horror&quot; element of VTM, so became curious on Removing the CAMP which is omnipresent in a lot of early CWOD (Anniversary editions allready killed a lot of it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-26-2014, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T18:16:49-07:00","id":293334,"title":"","content":"It may have been well for a storyteller to suffer and be burdened by OWoD's camp. I, however, rejoice in great camp as my great consolation.<br /> <br /> Realtalk though, camp is one of OWoD's guilty pleasures, within reason (Revised CoG are terrible). Though you can play serious campaign through OWoD, eliminating camp absolutely and completely would be eliminating OWoD itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T18:50:18-07:00","id":293340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod#post293308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...Anniversary editions allready killed a lot of it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was my answer. Heh. I was going to say that V20 (and the other *20 editions.) removed a lot of, what I would consider, excess camp. However, I agree with Katsura. cWoD is camp. I run mostly nWoD, but I've tended to use a lot of the concepts from cWoD because of the camp, and since the 20's I tend to use NWoD rules with cWoD setting for Vampire. (my opinion on other games depends, I like the nWoD versions of others more than cWoD, and cWoD better than nWoD) While I love Requiem, it really is the core of VtM with out the camp. Despite how much I love all of OP's work, I always found that Vampire lost something with that.<br /> <br /> So in a long, rambly way, I'm agreeing with Katsura, and pointing towards NWoD if you want to see some of what WoD without most of the camp looks like. I, persoanlly, champion using both to your taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T22:42:14-07:00","id":293449,"title":"","content":"Get rid of the Tribal divisions and cliques in Werewolf. Problem solved! (^VVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T23:35:11-07:00","id":293524,"title":"","content":"HA<br /> HA<br /> HA<br /> <br /> Very amusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T23:49:06-07:00","id":293531,"title":"","content":"Let's put out a guide to oWoD without the racism. I'm not sure how much would be left, especially regarding Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T02:32:58-07:00","id":293578,"title":"","content":"Technically Red Talons are not racist. They are specieist. Though they insistence on lupus members not having any homid ancestry reminds me of something. I bet one of leaders of Predator Kings is 1/16 homid or something. They seem to have enough of inferiority complex for that./<br /> <br /> But the best thing in one Gangrel books was a black man getting lynched by Ku Klux Klan, Embraced by a Gangrel, trying to get revenge on Ku Klux Klan guy only to be ripped apart by his Werewolf waifu. I bet they were Get of Fenris Kin. I would totally gun for blond Get waifu since I like blondes, but I don't know what would be their reaction to me being part Jew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-27-2014, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T07:48:29-07:00","id":293719,"title":"","content":"Early Werewolf was clumsily written with little research and contained the old Fianna and Get of Fenris Tribebooks. Later Werewolf had people who started doing research and, starting with the old Silver Fangs Tribebook, had the Silver Fangs be natively present over a far wider stretch than Russia, with far more diverse rolls among Garou royalty in North Africa, the Middle East, and most of Asia (including India and on into Indonesia).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the Silent Striders still ended up shackled to the Robert E. Howard vision of Set on into W20. But V20 Dark Ages made some changes on that front (as opposed to V20), so perhaps in time, that can get shifted around to make sense under legendry not distorted by one of H.P. Lovecraft's friends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=293578#post293578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically Red Talons are not racist. They are specieist. Though they insistence on lupus members not having any homid ancestry reminds me of something. I bet one of leaders of Predator Kings is 1/16 homid or something. They seem to have enough of inferiority complex for that./</div> </div> </div> </div>Most wouldn't even think that any of their tribe would have human ancestry, because it isn't something wolves do. The reaction would be, &quot;This is a thing for us?&quot; Also, the name of the camp is the Lodge of the Predator Kings. They are sunshine and smiles compared to the Dying Cubs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the best thing in one Gangrel books was a black man getting lynched by Ku Klux Klan, Embraced by a Gangrel, trying to get revenge on Ku Klux Klan guy only to be ripped apart by his Werewolf waifu. I bet they were Get of Fenris Kin. I would totally gun for blond Get waifu since I like blondes, but I don't know what would be their reaction to me being part Jew. </div> </div> </div>For any Fenrir that aren't the Swords of Heimdall, none would care, but a few with sympathies running thatway might turn a blind eye if some Swords-leaning Fenrir caused trouble, much as in many racist colonial societies that deny that they are racist - a flaw of their human upbringing rather than an ideal of their Tribal Totem. Of course, the overwhelming majority of Fenrir were against the Swords and in the Revised Tribebook it was revealed that the Swords had come down with a case of being torn apart by the rest of the tribe for being racist tools and no longer existed out in the open, or in any significant numbers. And anyone with sympathies to the Camp keeps their thoughts to themselves or ends up the same. The Revised Tribebook also explicitly noted that there were Fenrir from a number of non-European sources, and the Galliard template character was black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T07:54:31-07:00","id":293724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod#post293308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas on Rule changes and aspects to emphasize or deemphasize, if I want a more serious and less campy CWOD?<br /> <br /> Saw several ideas on &quot;Removing the horror&quot; element of VTM, so became curious on Removing the CAMP which is omnipresent in a lot of early CWOD (Anniversary editions allready killed a lot of it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Play New WOD. Done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T08:00:37-07:00","id":293729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For any Fenrir that aren't the Swords of Heimdall, none would care, but a few with sympathies running thatway might turn a blind eye if some Swords-leaning Fenrir caused trouble, much as in many racist colonial societies that deny that they are racist - a flaw of their human upbringing rather than an ideal of their Tribal Totem. Of course, the overwhelming majority of Fenrir were against the Swords and in the Revised Tribebook it was revealed that the Swords had come down with a case of being torn apart by the rest of the tribe for being racist tools and no longer existed out in the open, or in any significant numbers. And anyone with sympathies to the Camp keeps their thoughts to themselves or ends up the same. The Revised Tribebook also explicitly noted that there were Fenrir from a number of non-European sources, and the Galliard template character was black. </div> </div> </div>Of course I'm stereotyping for the sake of exaggaration.<br /> <br /> Though, I have this in mind:<br /> <br /> 1) Port Swords of Heimdall as one of local Werewolf minifactions to NWoD<br /> 2) Make them antagonists in Hunter: Vigil game with Loyalist of Thule PC(s).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T21:08:04-07:00","id":295599,"title":"","content":"Really, if you don't like camp, then Werewolf is not the game for you. I mean, a Captain Planet mega-corporation that wants to pollute the environment and sells demon possessed toys to make kids more violent. Nazi werewolves, feminazi werewolves, hippie werewolves, drunken Irish werewolves, martial arts werewolves, high tech urban werewolves, the list goes on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T21:12:57-07:00","id":295601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=295599#post295599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, if you don't like camp, then Werewolf is not the game for you. I mean, a Captain Planet mega-corporation that wants to pollute the environment and sells demon possessed toys to make kids more violent. Nazi werewolves, feminazi werewolves, hippie werewolves, drunken Irish werewolves, martial arts werewolves, high tech urban werewolves, the list goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You described first edition. It's a common mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T21:21:09-07:00","id":295602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=295601#post295601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You described first edition. It's a common mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen any evidence that these issues were substantially improved between editions. They have might smoothed down the Tribal stereotypes slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T21:55:44-07:00","id":295624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=295602#post295602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't seen any evidence that these issues were substantially improved between editions. They have might smoothed down the Tribal stereotypes slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you have a lot of reading to do from late second edition to W20*. Also, Pentex is, by and large, not really a camp thing. It's the sort of toxic attitude that produces rolling coal, writ large, What you think is in the arena of camp supervillainy is just escalating an extreme position in the manner the &quot;worse than real life&quot; of the setting does. This produces an effect similar to Poe's Law, where actual extreme positions are so extreme that they seem unreal. If only.<br /> <br /> *Skip Children of Gaia Revised, though. It's as bad as the earlier Fianna and Get of Fenris books. I'd say that the point of turnaround is about the time of the first Silver Fangs tribebook, which does away with the notion that they're all from Russia by introducing regional Houses of Fangs across North Africa, the Middle East and Asia. Slow, but the turnaround point isn't the end by a long shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T07:17:15-07:00","id":295830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=295599#post295599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, if you don't like camp, then Werewolf is not the game for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>neither is roleplaying in general. Seriously, the whole activity revolves around a bunch of people playing pretend, throwing dice and acting like it's high theater. it doesn't matter if you're running a game with a lot of campy themes like dragonlance or a relatively low-camp one like Legend of the Five Rings; just the act of roleplaying is, itself, pretty damn campy, pretty equally across the board.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, a Captain Planet </div> </div> </div>Either you've never played Werewolf or you've never watched Captian Planet. Seriously, this comparison is so banal and ignorant, and its repetition doesn't make it any less so. it's based on the superficiality of &quot;captain planet thinks pollution is bad; Garou think pollution is bad. Garou are like captain planet!&quot; Yeah, Garou think pollution is bad. So does everyone else in the world, I imagine (even the people doing the polluting don't want to be anywhere near the stuff, right?)<br /> <br /> Thing is, Captain Planet never actually hurts anyone. I don't think he even <i>punches</i> another living being through the entire run of the show. The show presents pollution as bad because it's ugly and the villains like it, not because of the actual harm it causes. Except to Captain Planet himself who is weakened by pollution, which is a stupid weakness for a pollution-fighting hero (but how else are you going ot inject even a little tension into a series otherwise utterly devoid of it, I guess). At the end of each 20-minute episode, everything is at rights again. The Captain has cleaned it all up, the Planeteers are back at home base, wheeler cracks a joke, they laugh, roll credits.<br /> <br /> Werewolf... isn't like that. First off, obviously, werewolves kill things - very often those things are people. Very often those people aren't even really the bad guys, they're low-paid mooks who just happen to be in the way at the moment. And very often, the Garou <i>just don't care</i>. Pollution isn't te only &quot;villain&quot; the Garou face, either - and when they do, its full effects are not only shown, but magnified. What doyou suppose Three Mile Island looks like in hte umbra? werewolf will show you, Ted Turner sure won't. No, Garou face problems from all over - the slow, griding erasure of their culture, as well as, very often those of their kinfolk for example. How often does Captain Planet deal with cultural genocide? Probably not often. Actual genocide? Probably never. However, these are defining conflicts for several werewolf tribes. How about Rage? When the Planeteers summon Captain Planet, do you think he has to consciously restrain himself from cleansing the earth of them, along with the rest of humanity, leaving a pure and pristine world for his patron? He doesn't. But give a Garou the sort of power that guy has, and see what happens. (THough, here's an interesting article about if Captain Planet DID have that going on... <a href=\"http://www.slacktory.com/2012/06/captain-planet-ma-ti-most-important-planeteer/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.slacktory.com/2012/06/cap...ant-planeteer/</a> )<br /> <br /> And of course,there's no happy ending in werewolf. Okay, you blew up the pesticide plant... Now what/ Does everything go back to being hunky-dory/ well no, now the town is out of work. The people there get desperate. You traded one problem for another. Oh, and of course all that burning pesticide created even more toxic problems... Good Job, Heroes. But wait, you don't have time to try to fix it; one of your sept elders thinks you need to go help another allied sept on some bug-hunt, for political reasons. So that polluted, desperate town will have to wait until you get back... assuming of course, you don't die. Which you very well might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mega-corporation that wants to pollute the environment </div> </div> </div>Most coirporations do pollute. Many of them quite greviously. You don't need the Wyrm involved for Endron to do what Endron does; just look at our world, the stuff Exxon does, or how Shell behaves in Nigeria and Sudan You can run chronicle after chronicle of werewolves dealing with the after-effects of corporate behavior, and never once, not <i>once</i> use the Wyrm except as a periphial threat, much less pentex.<br /> <br /> all Pentex does is create a unifying plot hook; Instead of <i>just</i> wasteful, harmful businesses, now you've got those same wasteful,harmful businesses that happen to be woven into a conspiracy. At its most basic, Pentex is just a very small cult of <i>very</i> wealthy businessmen who invest in each other' companies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and sells demon possessed toys to make kids more violent. </div> </div> </div>As noted, this has gone far more low-key in W20; it turns out the actual way toys are presented - categorically gendered, with &quot;boy&quot; toys emphasizing violence and strength and &quot;girl&quot; toys being bland and basic and often reinforcing poor body image... are already corrosive enough.<br /> <br /> Know why there's the occasional bane slipped in? Again, plot hooking; your character probably doesn't even <i>think</i> about the Anorexia Amy doll his neice is playing with, until he happens to poke into the umbra and see a starving little imp sitting on the same shelf, in the same place... It's a hook, usedto lure the player character into exploring what is, actually a pretty complex issue that - again - has no clear solution or resolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nazi werewolves, feminazi werewolves, hippie werewolves, drunken Irish werewolves, martial arts werewolves, high tech urban werewolves, the list goes on. </div> </div> </div>sort of like the Captain planet thing, these stereotypes are cheap, easy, and wholly inaccurate, and reflect someone whose knowledge of the game amounts to &quot;I glanced at a book once.&quot; it's the equivalent of thinking that becuase there are dwarves and elves in D&amp;D, then D&amp;D must be about fixing shoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T20:43:33-07:00","id":296506,"title":"","content":"A problem with accusations of Racism... I've seen accusations thrown around on spurious evidence.<br /> <br /> Read some forums recently that say &quot;Sailor moon is not ethnicly Diverse, therefore the anime is Racist&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T22:25:12-07:00","id":296586,"title":"","content":"Racism is hardly camp. It's very much part and parcel of the &quot;Darkness&quot; part of the World of <i>Darkness</i>. Make that Philodox/Elder/whatever work hard at her job. One can't simply go, &quot;I'm not a racist and I'll kill anyone who calls me such!&quot;<br /> <br /> Actually, that can be just as damning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T22:33:08-07:00","id":296594,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call the problem racism so much as camp. The Nazi werewolves were actually the least objectionable of what I listed, because in a way I think that Nazi werewolves make sense and are thematic. They are only silly when you look at all of the other silly tribe stereotypes. Ironically, the Nazi werewolves were the one thing which were removed, which actually added to the camp in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T00:02:51-07:00","id":296702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=296594#post296594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call the problem racism so much as camp. The Nazi werewolves were actually the least objectionable of what I listed, because in a way I think that Nazi werewolves make sense and are thematic. They are only silly when you look at all of the other silly tribe stereotypes. Ironically, the Nazi werewolves were the one thing which were removed, which actually added to the camp in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't make all that much sense. In fact, none of the camps other then the Fangs of Garm* and perhaps the Hand of Tyr** really make sense. That grab bag of Aesir and Vanir names represent the enemies of the Fenrir, not figures of reverence. What's more, the Get are proud of being werewolves, not so much from an association with a group of humans. They could go and settle down with any ethnic group; it wouldn't matter to them, since they're children of Fenris, and as long as they stay true to their painfully high standards which humans are not capable of reaching, they remain Fenrir.<br /> <br /> So along comes colonial racist bullshit, just a few centuries ago, and an interest in pre-Christian culture. Some Fenrir make a Camp out of it and name it after one of their ancient enemies. That only makes sense if they have a heaping helping of self-hatred. They're basically traitors, from the Get point of view, and traitors are not to be coddled, but killed. And so the Get who weren't racist tools, and the ones who might be but knew which way the wind was blowing, gathered together to turn the camp into an underground fringe group.<br /> <br /> *One of the brood of Fenris.<br /> **As in, &quot;Fenris took his hand, we'll get the rest.&quot; Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T02:10:06-07:00","id":296795,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to call it here and say The Cat Came Back won this thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:56:45-07:00","id":297525,"title":"","content":"I still claim Cheiron is far more sinister than Pentex in its now toned down take, because in the latter's cause we know they serve cosmic evil in the end. About Cheiron we don't have any clue apart from various rumors (I personally like that one with their Board of Directors being alien Hunters that failed Vigil at their own homeworld and might try to prevent same fate on Earth through highly questionable means)<br /> <br /> Of course I'm not saying Pentex is not a good antagonist material, just feels less mysterious unless our STs twist it so our expectations are on met.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-30-2014, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T15:27:41-07:00","id":297549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=295830#post295830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Either you've never played Werewolf or you've never watched Captian Planet. Seriously, this comparison is so banal and ignorant, and its repetition doesn't make it any less so. it's based on the superficiality of &quot;captain planet thinks pollution is bad; Garou think pollution is bad. Garou are like captain planet!&quot; Yeah, Garou think pollution is bad. So does everyone else in the world, I imagine (even the people doing the polluting don't want to be anywhere near the stuff, right?)<br /> <br /> Thing is, Captain Planet never actually hurts anyone. I don't think he even <i>punches</i> another living being through the entire run of the show. The show presents pollution as bad because it's ugly and the villains like it, not because of the actual harm it causes. Except to Captain Planet himself who is weakened by pollution, which is a stupid weakness for a pollution-fighting hero (but how else are you going ot inject even a little tension into a series otherwise utterly devoid of it, I guess). At the end of each 20-minute episode, everything is at rights again. The Captain has cleaned it all up, the Planeteers are back at home base, wheeler cracks a joke, they laugh, roll credits.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>WtA is more like the Don Cheadle Captain Planet: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TwJaELXadKo\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TwJaELXadKo</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T21:33:29-07:00","id":297787,"title":"","content":"Like I've written multiple times here, the 1st ed WtA (or,hell, ANY oWoD game) was written not only in a very different time peroid, but also in a different style. Back then, I honestly think most garou were assumed to be American born and based on stereotypes that were listed here. The Get were neo-nazi because germanic roots and the aryan ideals both fit the 'edgy' idea of a tribe following Fenris, due to most American assosiocating with the Norse myths being based on Wagner's operas, and therefore both german AND nazi related. The actually norse ties were either not considered or were very distant.<br /> <br /> And you see the same way of thinking in early vampire,too. It was Gothic Punk in a different decade, not as considerate of...well, anything that much really.<br /> <br /> Now, come revised and 20th eds, and the oWoD stopped being so extreme. A lot of grey was put between the blacks and whites. Get became based on actual norse stuff, rather than the American view of them. That and with the realisation that if you are going to write about a culture, maybe you should research it (See Howlers in revised vs Howlers in W20).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T21:46:30-07:00","id":297791,"title":"","content":"Given modern rise of SJWs, I still adhere to my headcanon that many of younger Black Furies are tumblrettes now, with their male Kinfolk whiteknighting them over the web.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T23:23:19-07:00","id":297860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=297791#post297791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given modern rise of SJWs, I still adhere to my headcanon that many of younger Black Furies are tumblrettes now, with their male Kinfolk whiteknighting them over the web.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NoCazqoNgy4\" data-code=\"NoCazqoNgy4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NoCazqoNgy4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:44:11-07:00","id":298030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=297791#post297791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given modern rise of SJWs, I still adhere to my headcanon that many of younger Black Furies are tumblrettes now, with their male Kinfolk whiteknighting them over the web.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has Gamergate caused strife between Black Furies and Glass Walkers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 10-31-2014, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:54:28-07:00","id":298041,"title":"","content":"Meh. If Gary Gygax and writers for Dungeons and Dragons knew about the Eddas and Sagas, I would think the World of Darkness writers were familiar with them. I don't think Wagnerian dissonant wailing to what might be considered operatic &quot;music&quot; very much influenced the concept of the Get.<br /> <br /> From my very limited understanding - an understanding tainted by the players I knew back in the States which made me hate Werewolf at the time - the Get on one hand seemed like Scandinavians wielding bat'leths, and on the other hand &quot;kill everything and let the other Tribes sort them out.&quot; Cheesy stereotyping, to be sure. Is Loki a totem for the Ragabash? Racism didn't appear in there. That being said, I feel that when I did read about the camp that had those feelings, I thought it fleshed them out a bit more. Gave them an albatross around their neck. Mentioning something like this to said Stateside players, it was like stabbing a sacred cow. They would literally <i>shout</i> to defend a fictional concept. But as I see it now, with the rise of nationalistic political parties here in Europe, such feelings by the Get could be fostered and the cubs are more free to express their opinion with little retaliation. Considering, too, that the population is dwindling, any body not given to the Wyrm has to be tolerated. Hopefully they'll learn the stupidity of their ways.<br /> <br /> I can easily see Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs also harboring such sentiments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:59:34-07:00","id":298048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has Gamergate causing strife between Black Furies and Glass Walkers? </div> </div> </div>It was obviously ploy of Incognito.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T07:07:45-07:00","id":298094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=298041#post298041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. If Gary Gygax and writers for Dungeons and Dragons knew about the Eddas and Sagas, I would think the World of Darkness writers were familiar with them. I don't think Wagnerian dissonant wailing to what might be considered operatic &quot;music&quot; very much influenced the concept of the Get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the -music- per se, more the idea that Norse myths were tied to german language rather than the scandinavian ones. The damn 2nd ed tribebook had german chapter titles, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=298041#post298041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my very limited understanding - an understanding tainted by the players I knew back in the States which made me hate Werewolf at the time - the Get on one hand seemed like Scandinavians wielding bat'leths, and on the other hand &quot;kill everything and let the other Tribes sort them out.&quot; Cheesy stereotyping, to be sure. Is Loki a totem for the Ragabash? Racism didn't appear in there. That being said, I feel that when I did read about the camp that had those feelings, I thought it fleshed them out a bit more. Gave them an albatross around their neck. Mentioning something like this to said Stateside players, it was like stabbing a sacred cow. They would literally <i>shout</i> to defend a fictional concept. But as I see it now, with the rise of nationalistic political parties here in Europe, such feelings by the Get could be fostered and the cubs are more free to express their opinion with little retaliation. Considering, too, that the population is dwindling, any body not given to the Wyrm has to be tolerated. Hopefully they'll learn the stupidity of their ways.<br /> <br /> I can easily see Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs also harboring such sentiments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how I see it; Swords of Heimindal make perfect sense as a camp and as you say, are a great albatross for the tribe. I like the idea of darker camps and the camp's creation made sense in post-WWI germany.<br /> <br /> But the problem here isn't that its that one camp, it's that a lot of players and those who don't play the game treat the whole tribe as nazi or racial purists. The 2nd ed tribebook is mostly the source of that, with flaws like mixed-heritage and quotes about Shadow Lords linking them to jews. Even if its a fictional concept, it felt wrong to tie it to a strange view of the norse myths and racial purity.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T06:28:29-08:00","id":306632,"title":"","content":"What is &quot;camp&quot; and what part of VtM do you consider camp? AND what is racist about it? If a group of vampires hailed from a certain part of the world would they not be predominantly a certain race or creed? All descriptions of these clans state about the older members but point out those embraced in more modern times can come from any background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T06:37:10-08:00","id":306634,"title":"","content":"&quot;Camp&quot; is a faction of a Werewolf Tribe. Swords of Heimdall were really, really racist, given they were a walking Naziesque stereotype who saw only their Germanic Kin as worthy enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T02:46:14-08:00","id":307284,"title":"","content":"I... don't think that's the kind of camp discussed in the OP. In that term, &quot;camp&quot; is an exaggerated theatricality, or self-recognized tastelessness or 'hokeyness.&quot; it's the concept of being overdone, and done so intentionally rather than accidentally.<br /> <br /> For film examples, since htye're readily available: <i>Rocky Horror Picture show</i> is Camp. <i>Barbarella</i> is camp. <i>Caveman</i> 9the one with Dennis Quaid and Ringo Starr) is camp.<i>Batman &amp; Robin</i> is camp, as is the 1960's Adam West Batman serial. Most 80's cartoons are pretty campy - Captain Planet has been brought up and definitely counts, but have you ever seen <i>Thundarr the barbarian</i> or,hell, <i>He-Man</i>?<br /> <br /> Camp is a cultural style, related to pulp or kitsch, which are all usually considered &quot;cheesy.&quot; Expressed i nthe WoD, it mostly takes the form of clan / tribal / tradition stereotypes; the leather-clad biker brujah railing against the suit ventrue with the slicked hair, while the prima donna toreador and giggling malkavian watch.The very theme of the World of Darkness - &quot;Gothic-Punk&quot; is o overwrought and clearly dated, that it is by itself a campy feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 11-09-2014, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T03:26:37-08:00","id":307294,"title":"","content":"Jojo's Bizarre Adventure is an example of camp done in good way, though it has its share of creepy horror, reinforced by the fact the author knows his stuff, even published a book about horror genre and is hyperrealistic about injuries.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:29:27-08:00","id":307820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=307294#post307294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jojo's Bizarre Adventure is an example of camp done in good way, though it has its share of creepy horror, reinforced by the fact the author knows his stuff, even published a book about horror genre and is <b>hyperrealistic about injuries.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Surely not every injury. How did the abridged Phantom Blood put it?<br /> <br /> &quot;I've... broken every bone in my body...&quot;<br /> <br /> SEVERAL MONTHS LATER<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, I can't believe that I'm already 70% healed!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:53:26-08:00","id":308006,"title":"","content":"&gt;Abridged series<br /> &gt;It was his early days when kids looked like midget wrestlers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T04:47:23-08:00","id":308045,"title":"","content":"I see a lot of Nazi talk going in relation with the CAMP of OWoD. I think thats the incorrect focus for removing CAMP.<br /> <br /> Who cares? If you game isn't set in the time period who cares which faction or supernatural breed was with the nazis. They can be as campy &quot;BRUHAHAHA&quot; as you, the DM, wants them to be or they could be like &quot;yeah in the time period our faction though they weren't bad, it hindsight it was a horribly mistake but in the times it wasn't so clear as it is now&quot;<br /> <br /> For my take on how to remove camp i would say that first i don't think is a good idea. If you want an supper oppressive WoD where there is only darkness and and every person in it is soul crusher ultra serious drama. That\u00b4s NWoD.<br /> <br /> Okay then from the games i know of Werewolf and Mage.<br /> <br /> For werewolf i would suggest like the &quot;cat that came back&quot; Pentex is this unified evil corporation for evil sake as to give plot hook for the player. So get rid of pentex as a unified evil. Make more &quot;innocent evil&quot;. They do what they do for profit and the gentleman gamer is no longer a board member.<br /> <br /> Get rid of some camps of werewolf. Example that comes to mind are the Cyber Dogs from the glass walkers*. This is of course if you as a DM allow them in the first place. Get rid of the canon NPCs make your own. Its not really that hard to make good NPCs from all the tribe without resorting to stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Example: if you think the Wendigo/Uktena simplify to much the native people make them more like political factions instead of tribes. Im thinking along the lines of the Dreamspeaker in Mage. They share common belief and native blood but that's it.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia. You could play them as they are in truth. The lowest of the tribes. The BGs at least ask their member to be &quot;Fuck the man&quot; but the Cog are the riffraff of the other tribes. They take the werewolf who too broken to be in the other tribes but not so broken as to not be of use to the garou nation. The list goes on.<br /> <br /> Those are my suggestion for Werewolf, for mage well, revised took away almost all the wonder and CAMP from previous edition for better or worse. Guide to technocracy does a decent job of making them not so CAMP. Sons of Ether on the other hand i would say to get rid of whole steampunk/pulp factor and drive home how close they are to the technocracy and thus how little differences make them forever apart.<br /> <br /> The marauders can be CAMPY things like &quot;The Wolf&quot; for example but the books in revised make a good point of how to set them up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-10-2014, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T07:50:17-08:00","id":308212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=308006#post308006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Abridged series<br /> &gt;It was his early days when kids looked like midget wrestlers</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't greentext here and hope to get away with it. At any rate, the contention didn't have anything to do with Araki's early art, but about story portrayal of injuries. And Nazi cyborgs with machine guns popping out of their chests who make up part of the visual basis of Guile from Street Fighter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T08:54:06-08:00","id":308241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't greentext here and hope to get away with it. At any rate, the contention didn't have anything to do with Araki's early art, but about story portrayal of injuries. And Nazi cyborgs with machine guns popping out of their chests who make up part of the visual basis of Guile from Street Fighter. </div> </div> </div>How far you are, anyway? Because comparing part 8 and 1 it's difficult to believe it's technically the same manga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-10-2014, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:36:28-08:00","id":308346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\