quot;let's do something else&quot;, you might not want to play with those people. </div> </div> </div>Dunno, I would use Swords of Heimdall in Dudes of Legends style game. Especially if the chronicle takes part in Illinois.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T21:04:50-08:00","id":319592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=319264#post319264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dunno, I would use Swords of Heimdall in Dudes of Legends style game. Especially if the chronicle takes part in Illinois.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the Swords is a bit different than using the original Get of Fenris Tribebook. The former can be framed as dupes trying to create a perverted mythic history that's an affront to Fenris crossed with the last part of Breaking Bad. The latter forgets that the sort of structured white supremacy that the Swords were birthed from is very new compared to the Fenrir, and trying to make it an ancient secret society is a headslapping affair of extraordinary magnitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T06:48:59-08:00","id":325972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=317115#post317115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Animu taught me that being edgy is often linked with being chuuni and campy. WtA is a product of 90s after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wanted anime in my game I'd play exalted or Big Eyes Small Mouth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T08:11:28-08:00","id":326015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=325972#post325972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wanted anime in my game I'd play exalted or Big Eyes Small Mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a medium. There's enough that stands apart from the light, comedic fare to warrant noting this, and it'd probably do anyone working on WoD material good to watch Requiem From the Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T19:48:51-08:00","id":327586,"title":"","content":"I own many of the old books, and honestly I don't just think it was just old school writers being less culturally sensitive than they are today, but a hefty number of players took a hint of something, gathered their personal prejudices that they likely didn't even recognize, and ran with it. Yeah, stuff slipped in that was stupid or at least poorly thought-out, but at least half of it was people reading into things. I for one never got Get of Fenris = Nazis until years later someone at a LARP told me that was a thing; I always got they were dicks to other Garou, but that was from an arrogant superiority complex that might not be entirely undeserved, not because of racism.<br /> <br /> To make Werewolf specifically less campy, I would:<br /> <br /> -Remove some of the wackier aspects of being a Bone Gnawer. It's a tragic existence being an outsider.<br /> -Reduce some of the Glass Walkers' abilities with technology. I feel they have a place in a serious setting, and I don't want to cripple them, but they can ramp up the silly too fast.<br /> -Keep Stargazers; remove Kalindo. Werewolf martial arts are just a little too silly.<br /> -Pentex doesn't need to less evil in my mind, but I would remove some of the sillier and more pointless subsidiaries, of which there are only a handful; mostly Tellus, Avalon, and Black Dog. Black Dog is just parody, and while cute, I don't think it adds to the setting; role-playing as big business is kind of silly anyway. Tellus and Avalon don't really make sense with Pentex's stated goals. Toys that attack or hurt children would simply draw too much attention. Toys that encourage misery or bad behavior in children really just seems too long term - Pentex is a classically American company that would burn down the building next quarter to get an extra .02% this one.<br /> -Make Corax and Nuwisha a bit more somber. Remove some of the more offbeat Ratkin aspects and gifts. Rokea may be best excised entirely, or left as a myth of possibly made into something else.<br /> <br /> After that, it's just editing out some of the goofier gifts and fetishes as they come up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T21:28:02-08:00","id":327681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=327586#post327586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Keep Stargazers; remove Kalindo. Werewolf martial arts are just a little too silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recast it as a bunch of shapeshifting tricks, and it'd be great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rokea may be best excised entirely, or left as a myth of possibly made into something else. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xxSI1QsIo8g\" data-code=\"xxSI1QsIo8g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xxSI1QsIo8g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NoCazqoNgy4\" data-code=\"NoCazqoNgy4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NoCazqoNgy4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T02:58:50-08:00","id":328006,"title":"","content":"I want to preface this with noting that most of these points (minus fera and the Gnawer part) are all ready pretty much in effect in most online chat/forum games. So, if you want a realistic WtA experience, seek out those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=327586#post327586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Remove some of the wackier aspects of being a Bone Gnawer. It's a tragic existence being an outsider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Omega tribe doesn't mean outsider of the Nation. It just means the least of them. Gnawers hold Caerns and positions in septs, so they are hardly outsiders of the Nation. That, and a huge point about the Gnawers is that they have cultural reasons to be the bottom tribe. They are the ones that, over even Glass Walkers, try to make the lives of the regular people better. That, and being werewolves, they also don't have to worry about a lot of dangers in the street as much as humans would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=327586#post327586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Reduce some of the Glass Walkers' abilities with technology. I feel they have a place in a serious setting, and I don't want to cripple them, but they can ramp up the silly too fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 'silly' can be used to potray how much some have given up to become machines. I mean, think what kind of garou puts a technofetish in their stomach to have more bullets? Not a very healthy one. That, and these guys put spirits into machines as fetishes, it'd be strange if they didn't have crazy machine powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=327586#post327586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Keep Stargazers; remove Kalindo. Werewolf martial arts are just a little too silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hooboy, the Gazers have a lot more problems outside Kailindo. They have got own Silver Pack and all. But yes, Kailindo should be made into shapeshifting tricks. Though, in my opinion, the major problem with the tribe is that the Gazers are written as more self-sufficent and far less tied to the Nation than other tribes. While Klaivaskar is shared all across the Nation, Kailindo is this secret art that only Gazers know. Hell, Hengeyokai even says that most asian shifters -don't- use martial arts while shifted, so Gazers are even better than other eastern shifters.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:51:05-08:00","id":328847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=328006#post328006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to preface this with noting that most of these points (minus fera and the Gnawer part) are all ready pretty much in effect in most online chat/forum games. So, if you want a realistic WtA experience, seek out those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistic, no. You can't have realism and magical animistic animal people who laugh at conservation of mass. Less camp, maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Omega tribe doesn't mean outsider of the Nation. It just means the least of them. Gnawers hold Caerns and positions in septs, so they are hardly outsiders of the Nation. That, and a huge point about the Gnawers is that they have cultural reasons to be the bottom tribe. They are the ones that, over even Glass Walkers, try to make the lives of the regular people better. That, and being werewolves, they also don't have to worry about a lot of dangers in the street as much as humans would. </div> </div> </div>Not outsiders to the nation, but definitely outsiders on their human half, and there is a whole slew of problems that poverty brings with it that even a werewolf isn't going to be able to handle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 'silly' can be used to portray how much some have given up to become machines. I mean, think what kind of garou puts a technofetish in their stomach to have more bullets? Not a very healthy one. That, and these guys put spirits into machines as fetishes, it'd be strange if they didn't have crazy machine powers. </div> </div> </div>Y'see, honestly I don't think that quite works thematically with Werewolf, at least not as an allied faction. A respect for technology and an attitude that it might not be all bad makes for a good counterpoint without wacky wacky technology powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hooboy, the Gazers have a lot more problems outside Kailindo. They have got own Silver Pack and all. But yes, Kailindo should be made into shapeshifting tricks. Though, in my opinion, the major problem with the tribe is that the Gazers are written as more self-sufficent and far less tied to the Nation than other tribes. While Klaivaskar is shared all across the Nation, Kailindo is this secret art that only Gazers know. Hell, Hengeyokai even says that most asian shifters -don't- use martial arts while shifted, so Gazers are even better than other eastern shifters. </div> </div> </div>The Stargazers might fit better into the game if less independent, but it's the wise Asian martial artist weirdness that gets campy. Honestly I'm not sure if I'm even comfortable with it being shape-shifting tricks, as it still implies Super Secret Oriental Knowledge and that's still kind of racist, even if less camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:52:49-08:00","id":329170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=328847#post328847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not outsiders to the nation, but definitely outsiders on their human half, and there is a whole slew of problems that poverty brings with it that even a werewolf isn't going to be able to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Bone Gnawer are thin and ragged, true. But they also have been living in poverty before poverty was even a concept. They've pretty much adapted to it, with gifts to get food and rites to make cardboard boxes into safe places. Most are homeless and try to avoid goverment as much as they can. For the ones in the countryside, I think they have rotting hovel towns and hunt their own food.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=328847#post328847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'see, honestly I don't think that quite works thematically with Werewolf, at least not as an allied faction. A respect for technology and an attitude that it might not be all bad makes for a good counterpoint without wacky wacky technology powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? The point of Glass Walkers is that they've sacrificed pretty much any advantage they once had for progress. They used to have ancestors, they used to have pure breed and they used to have mentors (though in W20, they still do have mentors). All of these were given up to be more modern and to fit in better with the humans. And so, they've replaced a lot of their old ties with new ones of technology. This includes spirits as well.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T07:41:19-08:00","id":329215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=328847#post328847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Stargazers might fit better into the game if less independent, but it's the wise Asian martial artist weirdness that gets campy. Honestly I'm not sure if I'm even comfortable with it being shape-shifting tricks, as it still implies Super Secret Oriental Knowledge and that's still kind of racist, even if less camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't have it be a Stargazer innovation. Just have it be ways in which some Garou fight, since more people than just one Stargazer are bound to notice the ramifications of changes in forms and implement them in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T15:25:17-08:00","id":329595,"title":"","content":"If i wanted a completely serious game, I'd play &quot;Customer Service: the Overworking&quot; and throw dice around for paying the water bill and finding something good to watch on TV.<br /> <br /> The WoD is a fantasy game. It's got a good deal of lampooning and satire in it - including self-satire - on top of the already fantastical elements. No matter what you do with it, it will <i>always</i> be one canister of goop away from being the original ninja Turtles comic book. There's no fixing it and frankly, I don't see any reason one would want to.<br /> <br /> WoD without camp is like AD&amp;D without Vancian magic and questionable laws of evolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T20:08:03-08:00","id":329827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=329595#post329595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i wanted a completely serious game, I'd play &quot;Customer Service: the Overworking&quot; and throw dice around for paying the water bill and finding something good to watch on TV.<br /> <br /> The WoD is a fantasy game. It's got a good deal of lampooning and satire in it - including self-satire - on top of the already fantastical elements. No matter what you do with it, it will <i>always</i> be one canister of goop away from being the original ninja Turtles comic book. There's no fixing it and frankly, I don't see any reason one would want to.<br /> <br /> WoD without camp is like AD&amp;D without Vancian magic and questionable laws of evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree with this assessment, on the grounds of an excluded middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:34:11-08:00","id":334511,"title":"","content":"Not to derail or start a holy war here, but &quot;AD&amp;D without Vancian magic&quot; is a bad example. It's called 5th Edition. If Wizards can revisit some of the oldest, most foundational parts of the game mechanics and create something that actually feels <u>more</u> true to its TSR roots than anything in the last twenty years, then pretty much anything is possible. And yeah...while tabletop anything is going to be high camp, a lot of online Werewolf groups trim it way down and turn it into something very different and also very good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T08:12:06-08:00","id":337037,"title":"","content":"To take from Star Trek, there is an idea: IDIC = Infinite Diversity in Infinite Combinations. What exactly is Camp, by definition: <i>v. tr</i>. To give a deliberately artificial, vulgar, or banal quality to: <i>camped up their cowboy costumes with chaps, tin stars, and ten-gallon hats.</i> (The American Heritage Dictionary). Growing up in a multicultural family (Cajun, Celtic, German, Indigenous Peoples, and Hispanic) I got the outsider-in view on a lot of what diversity is allowed and not allowed to mean. For instance, is John Wayne the hero who rides in to take care of those who need a hero, or the white man who interferes because the downtrodden minority in the film couldn't possibly be able to handle their own situation? I have heard arguments in both directions, so this is an academic and rhetorical question.<br /> <br /> The idea of camp seems to come from the question of perspective. One person's hero is another's stereotype. There is a food regularly served on the Pow-wow circuit called fry bread. Nothing about fry bread is indigenous. Some look on it as a symbol of oppression. Some see it as a symbol of surviving oppression. Many just see it as food or income. All these perspectives are correct in that they exist.<br /> <br /> Where I always get amused is that when one subgroup of society works to maintain the purity of their heritage as Indigenous Peoples, members of the Nations (i.e. followers of Santa Ria, Candomble, Lucumi), or maintain insular social communities such as Chinatown, etc. then it is Multicultural. But when a Werewolf tribal subgroup wants to do the same for their Germanic ancestral traditions it is being Nazi-esque.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it is that when a group is making up the stories that entertain them - they should express those elements they find entertaining. However, keep in mind that each stereo-type that is deliberately omitted is equally an expression of bias against someone else's hero. Infinite Diversity in Infinite Combination will provide a place for those they cannot stand as equally valuable to those whom they exalt. Besides, where is the real drama in only role-playing to that which we find comfortable and self-reinforcing?<br /> <br /> So, if your cowboy wants a ten-gallon hat, will they be allowed to wear one or have their dreams dashed because it is too campy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":".  Removed Asatru and replaced it with Germanic in order to make it fit the Splat. 12-11-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T08:30:46-08:00","id":337058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=337037#post337037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I always get amused is that when one subgroup of society works to maintain the purity of their heritage as Indigenous Peoples, members of the Nations (i.e. followers of Santa Ria, Candomble, Lucumi), or maintain insular social communities such as Chinatown, etc. then it is Multicultural. But when a Werewolf tribal subgroup wants to do the same for their Asatru ancestral traditions it is being Nazi-esque.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Swords of Heimdall aren't about preserving their heritage, though. They're about using a thin veneer of German folklore to be a white boy's club. Most Fenrir would be hesitant to consecrate a camp to an Aesir or Vanir deity, too, since those beings were the enemies of their totem and the tribe itself fought a long war against the Germanic deities, or some vampires and other monsters that had the same names, which often means the same thing in classic WoD games. Basically, Get of Fenris don't have a tradition of following Asatru. They have a tradition of being the boogiement of Asatru, because they're descended by spirit and blood from the greatest enemy of the &quot;All-Father&quot; that would break free and murder the Aesir at the Gotterdamerung. This, understandably, would rather dampen relations with people claiming to venerate Odin and company, for reasons beyond Rage putting the Asatru on edge because a monster walks among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T09:56:29-08:00","id":337148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=337058#post337058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, understandably, would rather dampen relations with people claiming to venerate Odin and company, for reasons beyond Rage putting the Asatru on edge because a monster walks among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed my point entirely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:17:21-08:00","id":337297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=337148#post337148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you missed my point entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I had two subjects to cover and they kind of bled into one another. I'll start again.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris, as of the Revised tribebook, frown on Germanic neopaganry. This has to do with Odin and company being among their greatest historical enemies*. Canonically, they look down on members of Camps that name themselves after Odin and co, disdaining Mjolinir's Thunder, the Glorious Fist of Wotan and others as being foolish at best and more likely to be unhinged dangers to everyone around. Fenrir tradition isn't like Asatru, it's like doing battle with people who practiced the traditions that Asatru tries to reconstruct. And likely killing them or leaving them horribly maimed.<br /> <br /> So really, it's not that Get of Fenris practicing Asatru is akin to Nazi-ism**, but that it makes no sense. They aren't viking werewolves. They're anti-viking werewolves. They're monsters that the followers of Germanic paganry feared and sought refuge from. They killed people in that area in droves for three millennia and didn't really let up too much even after the Impergium stopped. They're Gaian before they're Germanic.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Other than themselves.<br /> ** Unless they're Swords of Heimdall in the folkish sector, which apparently makes up a distressingly large amount of North American German neopagans at almost half or so.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">tl;dr Get of Fenris are monsters that don't follow human beliefs, and North American Germanic neopaganry is apparently lousy with militant racists.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-11-2014, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T05:12:25-08:00","id":337964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Other than themselves. </div> </div> </div>That's universal truth for Garou and maybe even Fera in general. Reading some accounts on their history there is lots of incompetence and proper lack of communication without which many things going on in default W20 setting could be prevented, but you know, that's the intentional design of developers which I understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T00:34:12-08:00","id":339809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=337297#post337297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Get of Fenris, as of the Revised tribebook, frown on Germanic neopaganry.&quot; ... &quot;They're anti-viking werewolves.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you didn't read the revised post. You got lost on the Asatru reference. Personally, I don't see those practicing the backhand side of a religion to be any different from that religion: From -1, through 0, to +1 - they all represent the same polarity. For example, one cannot be a Satanist without first admitting to the theology against which it is the practicing heckle-squad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So really, it's not that Get of Fenris practicing Asatru is akin to Nazi-ism**, but that it makes no sense. </div> </div> </div>Another member represented them as Nazi-esque because of their intolerance. Plots requiring good guys and bad guys must all be &quot;Nazi-esque&quot; whether one is attempting genocide through mollification of the belligerent through Peace and Love, Inc. or through brutality the entire point of coercing, convincing, or forcing others to change to the moral values held by a specific group is based in the effort to impose a specific ideology on others. Doing so with gas chambers or news articles is no less violent as the lines of the Venn Diagram are redrawn to demonstrate the value conquered. To some the Black Furies are champions of Gaia and the demonstration of Women's potential - to Rush Limbaugh, I am sure, they would just be another over powered group of feminazis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One of the points of my post is that anyone who praises a Germano-centric heritage is immediately a Nazi-istic hate monger, while those who promote the insular maintenance of any other heritage are cultural heroes defending themselves against the 0.009 to 0.021 percent of people of Germanic descent (all of whom are apparently stereotypes for wannabe Nazis). Infinite Diversity in Infinite Combination not only allows for combinations of various cultures as well as the maintenance of them in their more purified state. Thus Vulcans could serve in mixed ships as well as being on ships that were exclusively Vulcan (c.f. The U.S.S. T'Kumbra had an all-Vulcan crew. DS9 Season 7, Episode 4: Take me out to the Holosuite).<br /> <br /> So, my answer to the OP on the question of Camp was: What exactly do you consider camp for you and your group in the face of a world of varying perspectives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:16:28-08:00","id":340145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=339809#post339809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you didn't read the revised post. You got lost on the Asatru reference. Personally, I don't see those practicing the backhand side of a religion to be any different from that religion: From -1, through 0, to +1 - they all represent the same polarity. For example, one cannot be a Satanist without first admitting to the theology against which it is the practicing heckle-squad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not strictly true. Get of Fenris, again, are Gaian first and mix it up with a band of vampires and ghouls second - which they name only as enemies, and consistently mention humans being totally wrong about all sorts of things, as most tribes do. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satanism#Atheistic_Satanism\" target=\"_blank\">Also, some branches of Satanism don't have anything to do with Christianity as such.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another member represented them as Nazi-esque because of their intolerance. Plots requiring good guys and bad guys must all be &quot;Nazi-esque&quot; whether one is attempting genocide through mollification of the belligerent through Peace and Love, Inc. or through brutality the entire point of coercing, convincing, or forcing others to change to the moral values held by a specific group is based in the effort to impose a specific ideology on others. Doing so with gas chambers or news articles is no less violent as the lines of the Venn Diagram are redrawn to demonstrate the value conquered. To some the Black Furies are champions of Gaia and the demonstration of Women's potential - to Rush Limbaugh, I am sure, they would just be another over powered group of feminazis. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>And Rush Limbaugh isn't someone worth listening to, so why would you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the points of my post is that anyone who praises a Germano-centric heritage is immediately a Nazi-istic hate monger, while those who promote the insular maintenance of any other heritage are cultural heroes defending themselves against the 0.009 to 0.021 percent of people of Germanic descent (all of whom are apparently stereotypes for wannabe Nazis). </div> </div> </div>Probably because the other groups didn't actually build a military-industrial complex in the early 20th century that vowed to empty other countries for &quot;German living room&quot;. And likely weren't involved in Imperialism and colonialism. Or end up spawning a movement including a number of smaller groups around large parts of the world, such as the US, that have that ideology married to one of general &quot;white&quot; identity, combining the two bankrupt racial theories into one incredibly bankrupt racial theory.<br /> <br /> By the way, Germanocentrism isn't a heritage, unless you're talking about a long line of germanocentrists. Which probably crosses over into actual Nazism in the modern context and is likely to still be unpleasant even if it doesn't, because by definition, they think that German culture, people, etc should take primacy over everything else. That's what it means to be x-centric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Infinite Diversity in Infinite Combination not only allows for combinations of various cultures as well as the maintenance of them in their more purified state. Thus Vulcans could serve in mixed ships as well as being on ships that were exclusively Vulcan (c.f. The U.S.S. T'Kumbra had an all-Vulcan crew. DS9 Season 7, Episode 4: Take me out to the Holosuite). </div> </div> </div>But before that happens, the people with their boots on the necks of the ones they're standing on are going to have to get off. They might not even realize who or what they're standing on, but this doesn't change the state of affairs. Star Trek gets away with neutral talk because neither the Vulcans nor the Humans in charge attempted to colonize the homes of the other. Additionally, it posits a fictional setting where people are willing to let go of nationalism, which is so far off as to seem even less possible than FTL travel and the other sci-fi, often verging into science-fantasy, elements of the franchise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:20:40-08:00","id":340550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/293308-how-to-decamp-cwod?p=340145#post340145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not strictly true. Get of Fenris, again, are Gaian first and mix it up with a band of vampires and ghouls second - which they name only as enemies, and consistently mention humans being totally wrong about all sorts of things, as most tribes do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should substitute &quot;groups&quot; for &quot;tribes&quot;. This is not a werewolf thing, it is a social thing. There are certainly Indigenous Peoples with whom I have had no contact. But of the tribes with which I have had contact, all of them without missing a step, speak a language which defines anyone who is a member of their culture as 'the People' and anyone who is not a member of their group as 'Not People'. In many Middle Eastern text the same applies, those who belong to our city state are human, and those who do not are not human. I am not judging by the actions. I observe based on the function at its mean. If the conception has the same polarising identification of inside and outside then it is the same - whether it comes from a nationalistic deme or a quilting circle.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, some branches of Satanism don't have anything to do with Christianity as such. </div> </div> </div>Since your appealing to authority for your example, so will I. Rosemary Radford Ruether questioned whether or not those who ascribe a concept of their choice to a name of power do not risk waking up something that is neither what they believe and want it to be, nor nearly as fictional as their feelings of safety in using it may suppose. Simply declaring the Prosecuting Attorney, one which seeks to execute justice by might without consideration of circumstance or intent, of a religion to be the perfect emblem of one's self declared ethical hedonism neither makes that entity more or less real than it is nor does the use of it keep that use from representing the goals said entity expresses in order to increase condemnation by increasing the number who violate the Mandate of Heaven. Playing Angel's Advocate to the Devil's, this rationale is solid.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Rush Limbaugh isn't someone worth listening to, so why would you? </div> </div> </div>I remember a young radio anouncer in Kansas City who upon hearing that the City Counsel had passed a law to remove vagrants from the elite shopping area in which anyone who could not produce a certain amount of cash at the request of a police officer could be arrested. That young radio announcer railed against City Hall for their lack of support of the right of free people to go and be where they please, so long as they were peacefully behaved. That announcer was Rush Limbaugh. Do I agree with everything I have heard him say? No. Does he have all his 'facts' correct? No, I have heard him use errant and invalid data - which may not strictly be his fault as some information is not verrified for public use. Why would I listen to him? Because we do not live in a world of black and white, but in a world of living color with many highlights and shadows. Whether it is Rush Limbaugh, Louis Farrakhan, or Gustavo Guti\u00e9rrez Merino, Ordo Praedicatorum does not matter. They are all representatives of humanity.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably because the other groups didn't actually build a military-industrial complex in the early 20th century that vowed to empty other countries for &quot;German living room&quot;. And likely weren't involved in Imperialism and colonialism. Or end up spawning a movement including a number of smaller groups around large parts of the world, such as the US, that have that ideology married to one of general &quot;white&quot; identity, combining the two bankrupt racial theories into one incredibly bankrupt racial theory. </div> </div> </div>To quote Love and Rockets, &quot;Going against nature is a part of nature too&quot;, from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bo3R3LBjDek\" target=\"_blank\">No New Tale to Tell</a>. While it is natural to limit the idea of &quot;isms&quot; to those things pounded into us by a Military-Industrial-Edutainment Complex the greater view sees the interactions of the chemistry, where valence factors describe the solution and dissolution of ever interactive substances, in the same way that society forms and dissolves. Consider the song, &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7xxgRUyzgs0\" target=\"_blank\">Cult of Personality</a>&quot; by Living Colour: <div align=\"center\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I sell the things you need to be<br /> I'm the smiling face on your TV<br /> I'm the cult of personality<br /> I exploit you, still you love me<br /> I tell you one and one makes three&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm the cult of personality<br /> Like Joseph Stalin and Gandhi... </div> </div> </div></div> <br /> If one argues for evolution, then one must accept that the brutality of environment (including man) has been the nature of what we cannot avoid being since hundreds of thousands of years before written history. Yet, oddly enough a lame duck US President writes 14 points in which the validity of all groups competing for the limited resources of petri dish earth are declared to be valid and sacrosanct - and suddenly the world pretends this is the case. But while each nation, culture, gender, and all propose rational and peaceful co-existence is this not merely an excuse to bide their time while they find 'genteel' ways to eliminate their competitors in the the 'life boat'?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, Germanocentrism isn't a heritage, unless you're talking about a long line of germanocentrists. Which probably crosses over into actual Nazism in the modern context and is likely to still be unpleasant even if it doesn't, because by definition, they think that German culture, people, etc should take primacy over everything else. That's what it means to be x-centric. </div> </div> </div>In my own writings I separate a difference between Selfish and Self-centered. Objectivity is an impossibility. Neutrality invariably champions the losing side in order to make it seem equal to the victors and denigrates the victors as unworthy of their position in order to justify the loser. The only thing left is rationale. A rational observer will not be objective, neutral, nor selfish - but they cannot observe from any place other than the center of themselves. They are self-centered. To be Germano-centric, Celto-centric, Sino-centric, etc. is the rational observation of that influence which pervades the time and space of your existence. But there is not one place on the planet that does not contain militant complexes determined to exploit or eliminate others in their competition for use of the limited resources of our Petri Dish earth. Whether one considers the dark-side capitalism of the Cartels and Triad, the imposed nationalism of communists countries seeking to eradicate anything that does not conform to their declared standard, or the overbearing soccer mom determined to control the outcome of the game - they are no different from one another in nature.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But before that happens, the people with their boots on the necks of the ones they're standing on are going to have to get off. They might not even realize who or what they're standing on, but this doesn't change the state of affairs. Star Trek gets away with neutral talk because neither the Vulcans nor the Humans in charge attempted to colonize the homes of the other. Additionally, it posits a fictional setting where people are willing to let go of nationalism, which is so far off as to seem even less possible than FTL travel and the other sci-fi, often verging into science-fantasy, elements of the franchise. </div> </div> </div>There is absolutely no relinquishing of nationalism in Star Trek. There is a reality which Roddenberry understood, that Humanity is not humane. But he also understood that lacking the humane one can express and support the reality of what humanity is through comprehension, compassion, and tollerance. No group appears in any Star Trek episode or movie that does not represent that humanity. Whether Romulan, Klingon, Andorian, or Borg they all represent what it means to be human. They all represent, what in Mage is, the effort to Ascend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 12-15-2014, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}